/-!
# Adjoint ideals: restriction vanishing, asymptotic extension and section lifting

For a projective morphism `f : X ⟶ Z` to an affine scheme from a smooth variety over an
algebraically closed field of characteristic zero, a prime divisor `S` and the (reduced, then
asymptotic) adjoint ideal of a boundary along `S`, this file proves the restriction exact sequence
and the vanishing that makes restriction of twisted sections surjective, that the adjoint ideal is
a unit near points of multiplicity `< 1`, the extension of sections from `S` for asymptotic adjoint
ideals and its twisted forms, the global generation of the twisted asymptotic adjoint ideal, the
ample perturbation avoiding base loci, and finally the lifting of sections of
`𝒪_S(k(K_S + Ω))` to `𝒪_X(k(K_X + Δ))` below the restricted asymptotic fixed part.

## Main results

* `MMP.Fourfold.isReducedAdjointIdealOn_restriction_vanishing`: the restriction exact sequence
  of the reduced adjoint ideal along `S` and the vanishing of its twisted higher direct images.
* `IsReducedAdjointIdealOn.exists_nhds_eq_range_germToFunctionField_of_multiplicityAt_lt_one`:
  the adjoint ideal is the unit ideal near a point where the boundary has multiplicity `< 1`.
* `MMP.Fourfold.exists_isRestrictionAlong_of_linearlyEquivalent_add`: sections of the asymptotic
  adjoint ideal on `S` extend to `X`.
* `MMP.Fourfold.exists_isRestrictionAlong_of_exists_isRestrictionAlong_twist`: extension after a
  twist implies extension without it.
* `MMP.Fourfold.IsAsymptoticAdjointIdeal.generated_twist_canonical_add_ample_add_veryAmple`: the
  twisted asymptotic adjoint ideal is globally generated.
* `MMP.Fourfold.exists_notMem_baseLocusIn_of_forall_multiplicityAt_lt`: an ample perturbation
  whose base locus avoids the given points.
* `MMP.Fourfold.asymptoticAdjointIdeal_subset_and_exists_isRestrictionAlong`: asymptotic
  extension after one fixed ample twist.
* `MMP.Fourfold.exists_isRestrictionAlong_of_le_restrictedAsymptoticFixedPart`: sections of
  `𝒪_S(k(K_S + Ω))` lift to `𝒪_X(k(K_X + Δ))` below the restricted asymptotic fixed part.

## References

* [Hacon–McKernan, *Extension theorems and the existence of flips*]
* [J. Kollár, S. Mori, *Birational geometry of algebraic varieties*][KM98], Theorem 2.64
-/

@[expose] public section

